From 24193ca80f07d02156e02863bd720b94a6a07918 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom de Vries <tdevries@suse.de>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 15:32:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] [gdb/testsuite] Handle CSI ? 1034 l/h

On Tumbleweed aarch64-linux, I ran into:
...
Running gdb.tui/tui-mode-switch.exp ...
ERROR: unsupported
    while executing
"error "unsupported""
    (procedure "_csi_0x3f_l" line 21)
...

The test-case is the only TUI test-case that uses TERM=xterm.

The unsupported sequence is CSI ? 1034 l, meaning "Don't interpret meta
key" [1].

Fix this by ignoring the sequence.  While we're at it, likewise ignore its
counterpart CSI ? 1034 h.

Tested on aarch64-linux.

Bug: https://sourceware.org/bugzilla/show_bug.cgi?id=34720

[1] https://invisible-island.net/xterm/ctlseqs/ctlseqs.html
---
 gdb/testsuite/lib/tuiterm.exp | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/gdb/testsuite/lib/tuiterm.exp b/gdb/testsuite/lib/tuiterm.exp
index 9aa90c7d26c..d7290e3d5d2 100644
--- a/gdb/testsuite/lib/tuiterm.exp
+++ b/gdb/testsuite/lib/tuiterm.exp
@@ -705,6 +705,9 @@ proc Term::_csi_0x3f_h { args } {
 	    1006 {
 		_log "ignored: Enable SGR Mouse Mode"
 	    }
+	    1034 {
+		_log "ignored: Interpret meta key"
+	    }
 	    1049 {
 		_log "switch to alternate screen"
 		_set_alternate 1
@@ -734,6 +737,9 @@ proc Term::_csi_0x3f_l { args } {
 	    1006 {
 		_log "ignored: Disable SGR Mouse Mode"
 	    }
+	    1034 {
+		_log "ignored: Don't interpret meta key"
+	    }
 	    1049 {
 		_log "switch from alternate screen"
 		_set_alternate 0

base-commit: a83f6955ab525b5d151ad5ae74d70adad7d2b893
